The sandbox startup card and its log.

The chat showed one line while a sandbox started ("Connecting host…",
"Starting agent…"), and a generic error when it failed. With this
deployment's server (images/server/patches/0016-startup-progress.patch) the
session carries a record of its start, step by step. SandboxStartupCard shows
it in the thread, where that line was: each step with its time and what it's
waiting for, each repository's clone and setup script, and, when something
goes wrong, why in plain words with the failed container's log, Try again
(for a resumable host, like the environment menu's), Repository variables
for a clone problem, and Copy error details. "Log" opens the startup log,
polled from GET /v1/sessions/{id}/startup-log while the start is going, with
a filter per source. A finished start folds to "Sandbox ready in 30s" and
stays until the thread moves on after it: the agent works, or a new message
comes. So a start a message asked for goes when the agent gets to it, one no
message asked for (Start now, Try again) stays until the next message, and
one in the middle of a turn goes with the agent's next step. A failed setup
script stays until dismissed.
It sits above Working… and pending questions, since the start comes first.

The record arrives in the session snapshot (`startup`) and in session.startup
events (lib/sandboxStartup.ts, sse.ts, chatStore's sandboxStartup). The card
replaces the in-thread stage line and Working… while the sandbox starts, and
the failure band above the composer. Without a record (an older server) the
old line still shows.

Terminal-first sessions: while the sandbox starts, the terminal view counts
as starting up, so it offers no Resume session, which would only start
another wake. It shows the startup card instead, and a stale terminal's
overlay hides its Resume too.

The environment menu is unchanged.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0020-environment-menu.patch.
